(83, 'Whyte', 'UK', 1999, 'Established in 1999 Whyte is a British brand. John Whyte was a suspension designer at Benetton Formula One', 'https://whytebikes.com/'),
(84, 'Fezzari', 'USA', 2005, 'Founder Chris Washburn decided to quit his job, and in 2005, he went to work creating Fezzari Bicycles, a web-based company specializing in custom-designed, high-end bikes for both road and mountain riders', 'https://fezzari.com/'),
(85, 'Mondraker', 'Spain', 2001, 'founded by Paco Sanchez and Miguel Pina', 'https://mondraker.com/'),
(86, 'Rocky Mountain', 'Canada', 1981, 'Founder: Grayson Bain', 'https://intl.bikes.com/'),
(87, 'Argonaut', 'USA', 2014, 'Argonaut founder and owner Ben Farver', 'https://argonautcycles.com/'),
(88, 'Early Rider', 'UK', 2005, 'Began in a shed in Henley on Thames', 'https://earlyrider.com/'),
(89, 'Marin', 'USA', 1986, 'Marin founded by Bob Buckley, in Marin County, California', 'https://www.marinbikes.com/'),
(90, 'Husqvarna', 'Swedish', 1689, 'Husqvarna was founded near the town of Huskvarna in Sweden in 1689. The company started out as a maker of muskets, and the Husqvarna logo still depicts a gun sight viewed from the end of the barrel.', 'https://husqvarna-bicycles.com/'),
(91, 'No22', 'USA', 2012, 'Founded in 2012 by Bryce Gracey and Mike Smith, No. 22 Bicycle Company produces a line of titanium frames and complete custom bikes.', 'https://22bicycles.com/'),
(93, 'Vielo', 'UK', 2017, 'Founded by father and son, Ian and Trevor Hughes - Gateshead UK', 'https://www.vielo.cc/'),
(94, 'Reap', 'UK', 2014, 'Martin Meir, Founder & Managing Director', 'https://reapbikes.com/'),
(95, 'Diamondback', 'US', 1977, 'iamondback Bicycles was founded as a BMX brand in 1977 by Western States Imports in Newbury Park, California', 'https://www.diamondback.com/'),
(96, 'Pronghorn', 'Denmark', 2007, '', 'https://pronghornracing.com/'),
(97, 'Liv', 'Taiwan', 2008, 'Liv is the sister brand to Giant Bicycles and was created in 2008, founded by Bonnie Tu', 'https://www.liv-cycling.com/'),
(98, 'Moots', 'US', 1981, 'Moots Cycles is an American bicycle manufacturer located in Steamboat Springs, Colorado. Founded in 1981 by Kent Eriksen', 'https://moots.com/'),
(99, 'Yeti', 'US', 1985, 'Yeti Cycles was founded in 1985 by John Parker in California, when mountain biking was gaining in popularity. Parker was a welder who built movie sets in Hollywood and later became a mountain bike designer and racer.', 'https://yeticycles.com/'),
(100, 'Propain', 'Germany', 2006, 'Founded by Robert Krauss and Markus Zander in 2006', 'https://www.propain-bikes.com/'),
(101, 'Octane One', 'Poland', 0, '', 'https://octane-one.com/'),
(102, 'Origine', 'France', 0, 'Direct sales', 'https://www.origine-cycles.com/'),
(103, 'Winspace', 'China', 2008, 'Founded 2008 - Based in Xiamen, China', 'https://www.winspace.cc/'),
(104, 'All-City', 'USA', 2007, 'It was founded in 2007 by Quality Bicycle Products (QBP)', 'https://allcitycycles.com/'),
(105, 'Planet X', 'UK', 1988, 'Planet X is a bicycle company based in Rotherham, in the north of England. It was founded in 1988 by Dave Loughran and, in 2020, became an employee-owned trust.', 'https://www.planetx.co.uk/'),
(106, 'Northroad', 'UK', 2016, 'NorthRoad Founders Ian and Jane set up a small workshop in their shed', 'https://www.northroadcycles.com/'),
(107, 'Bombtrack', 'Germany', 2013, 'Independent bicycle company based in Cologne', 'https://www.bombtrack.com/'),
(108, 'Baum', 'Australia', 1996, 'Handmade bicycles in both titanium and steel since 1996 - Founded by Darren Baum', 'https://baumcycles.com/'),
(109, 'Fondriest', 'Italy', 1998, 'After a back injury forced him into early retirement in 1998, he founded the Fondriest brand with his brother Francesco, concentrating primarily on producing bespoke handmade carbon fibre road racing bikes.', 'https://www.fondriestbici.com/'),
(110, 'Eurobike', '', 0, '', ''),
(111, 'Van Nicholas', 'Netherlands', 2006, 'Began life as a Dutch family company before becoming part of the famous Dutch bike brand Koga in 2012.', 'https://www.vannicholas.com/'),
(112, 'Litespeed', 'USA', 1986, 'Litespeed is a U.S. bicycle manufacturer founded in 1986 in Ooltewah, Tennessee by David Lynskey and later sold in 1999.', 'https://litespeed.com/'),
(113, 'GT', 'USA', 1972, 'GT was founded in 1972, by Gary Turner and Richard Long in Santa Ana, California, and was noted at its inception for spearheading the prominence of BMX bicycles', 'https://www.gtbicycles.com/'),
(114, 'Lynskey', 'USA', 2006, 'Lynskey Performance Designs LLC is a titanium bicycle designer and manufacturing company based in Chattanooga, Tennessee, founded and currently operated by the Lynskey family, who began building titanium bicycles in 1984.[1] The family founded the company Litespeed Titanium, which they sold in 1999.', 'https://lynskeyperformance.com/'),
(115, 'Mosaic', 'US', 2010, 'Mosaic Cycles is a bicycle manufacturer based in Boulder, Colorado. It was founded in 2010 by Aaron Barcheck and Ryan Cannizzaro. The company is known for its high-end custom-made steel and titanium bikes, which are handcrafted in its Colorado workshop. Mosaic Cycles offers a range of road, cyclocross, and mountain bikes, as well as a selection of bike frames and forks.', 'https://www.mosaiccycles.com/'),
(116, 'Lapierre', 'France', 1946, 'The company was founded in 1946 by Gaston Lapierre in Dijon.', 'https://www.lapierrebikes.com'),
(117, 'Chapter 2', 'New Zealand', 2017, 'Chapter2 was founded by father and son duo Neil and Mike Pryde in Auckland, New Zealand in 2017. The pair has +75 years of combined experience in Sporting Goods and Industrial Design.', 'https://www.chapter2bikes.com'),
(118, 'Bold', 'Switzerland', 2014, 'Founded in 2014 by Vincenz Droux, Bold Cycles manufactures mountain bikes based on its patented Internal Suspension Technology, which enables the company to place the shock inside the full carbon frame. Sold majority stake to Scott Sports Group 2019.', 'https://www.boldcycles.com'),
(119, 'Bergamont', 'Germany', 1993, 'Bergamont is a German bicycle manufacturer that was founded by Stefan Berkes in St. Pauli, Hamburg in 1993. Now owned by Scott Sports', 'https://www.bergamont.com'),
(120, 'Moda', 'UK', 2009, 'Lancashire based company', 'https://www.moda-bikes.com'),
(121, 'Apollo Bicycles', 'Australia', 1978, 'Designing bikes for Australia and the world since 1978', 'https://www.apollobikes.com'),
(122, 'Handsling', 'UK', 2014, 'Handsling Bikes started life in 2014 when the race team, Handsling Racing, needed new frames. Rather than seek a new sponsor, Simon Whiten set out to use his contacts in the Far East to manufacture bespoke frames. Handsling Bikes is in Oakhanger, Hampshire.', 'https://handslingbikes.com'),
(123, 'State', 'US', 2009, 'Founded by Mehdi Farsi and Reza Farsi in 2009. The brand started as a manufacturer of cheap fixed-gear and single-speed steel bikes', 'https://www.statebicycle.com'),
(124, 'Koga', 'Netherlands', 1974, 'The company was founded by Andries Gaastra in 1974. The name Koga is a combination of his surname and that of his wife Marion Kowallik.', 'https://www.koga.com'),
(125, 'Priority', 'US', 2012, 'Priority Bicycles is an American bicycle manufacturer based in New York City. The company was founded in 2012 by Dave Weiner, who quit his job as North American CEO of a software company to start a bicycle company.', 'https://www.prioritybicycles.com'),
(126, 'Jaegher', 'Beligan', 1934, 'Jaegher is a Belgian brand of handmade bicycles. Founded in 1934 by Odiel Van Eenooghe, who began building bicycles in his workshop in Ruiselede. The name Jaegher comes from the Dutch word "jager," which means "hunter."', 'https://www.jaegher.be'),
(127, 'Dare', 'Taiwan', 2012, 'Dare Bikes is a Taiwanese bicycle manufacturer that was founded in 2012 by a group of experienced engineers and designers. The company is based in Taichung, Taiwan, which is known as the "bicycle capital of the world" due to the high concentration of bicycle manufacturers in the city.', 'https://darebikes.eu'),
(128, 'Lauf', 'Iceland', 2010, 'Lauf Cycling is an Icelandic bicycle brand based in Reykjavik, Iceland. Founded by Benedikt Skulason and Gudberg Bjornsson.', 'https://www.laufcycling.com'),
(129, 'Fara', 'Norway', 2016, 'Fara Cycling was founded in Stjørdal, Norway 2016 by Jeff Webb.', 'https://faracycling.com'),
(130, 'Corratec', 'Germany', 1990, 'Corratec is a German bicycle company that was founded in 1990 by Konrad Irlbacher. The company started out as a small workshop in Bavaria, Germany, where Irlbacher developed and built his first bike frames by hand.', 'https://www.corratec.com'),
(131, 'Silverback', 'South Africa', 2004, 'Silverback Bikes is a South African bicycle brand that was founded in 2004 by Deon Retief', 'https://silverbackbikes.de'),
(132, 'Atherton', 'UK', 2019, 'Founded by Siblings Dan, Gee and Rachel Atherton. Between them they hold 49 World Cups, 8 World Championships and 7 World Cup Overalls.', 'https://www.athertonbikes.com'),
(133, 'Rambo', 'US', 2015, 'To feel BadAss, one must be BadAss and there’s no better way to be a BadAss then owning a BadAss Bike….just sayin!', 'https://www.rambobikes.com'),
(134, 'Berria', 'Spain', 2012, 'Berria Bikes was born in 2012 by brothers José and David Vitoria.', 'https://berriabikes.com'),
(135, 'Mason', 'UK', 2014, 'There are easy ways to make a bicycle and bring it to market and then theres the MASON way', 'https://masoncycles.cc'),
(136, 'Isaac', 'Netherlands', 2001, 'In 2001, a group of fanatical bicycle enthusiasts got together and started Isaac Cycle. We were convinced that everything could be improved.', 'https://www.isaac-cycle.com'),
(137, 'J.Laverack', 'UK', 2015, 'Where does the name J.Laverack come from? Co-founder Oliver Laverack says the company, and the first model, is named after his grandad.', 'https://www.jlaverack.co.uk'),
(138, 'Fairlight', 'UK', 2016, 'Founders Dom Thomas and John Reid. Prior to co-founding Fairlight Cycles, Dom Thomas was designing and hand-building custom and small-scale production frames for his own brand Wold Cycles. He was also the lead bike designer and brand manager for Genesis Bikes.', 'https://fairlightcycles.com'),
(139, 'Blue', 'US', 2004, 'Blue Competition Cycles with its president Orli Chinea Martin established new headquarters in 2018 with its offices and warehouse now located near Boulder, Colorado', 'https://rideblue.com'),
(140, 'Salsa', 'US', 1982, 'Ross Shafer founded Salsa Cycles in the early 1980s. The company initially focused on producing bicycle frames and custom stems. In 1997, the brand was acquired by Minnesota-based Quality Bicycle Products', 'https://www.salsacycles.com'),
(141, 'Brodie', 'Canada', 1986, 'Paul Brodie started Brodie Research and Technology in 1986, after leaving his frame building position with Rocky Mountain Bicycles, manufacturing custom steel hardtail mountain bikes.', 'https://www.brodiebicycles.com'),
(142, 'Baldiso', 'Germany', 2020, 'Sebastian Baldauf, ex- professional cyclist and former German mountain champion, founded the bicycle brand BALDISO in 2020', 'https://www.baldiso.com'),
(143, 'Dosnoventa', 'Spain', 2012, 'Dosnoventa Was Founded In Barcelona In 2012 By A Group Of Like-minded Individuals. We Create High-quality, Efficient And Long-lasting Bicycles With A Strong Identity For Contemporary Riding.', 'https://dosnoventabikes.com'),
(144, 'Hope', 'UK', 1989, 'Since 1989, owners Ian Weatherill and Simon Sharp have been pushing the industry forward through designing, testing and manufacturing virtually all products in-house at the factory in Barnoldswick, United Kingdom.', 'https://www.hopetech.com'),
(145, 'Unno', 'Spain', 2012, 'Unno Bikes, a company based in Barcelona, Spain, is spearheaded by Cesar Rojo, an engineer and former World Cup downhill racer. The company is recognized for its innovative and groundbreaking designs in mountain biking, particularly for pioneering the "long and slack" geometry now widely adopted in the industry. Unno Bikes began its journey in August 2012, inspired by a desire for disruptive and innovative designs, and by September 2012, they were developing their first downhill frame. Their approach emphasizes the importance of every detail in bike design, believing that bikes are not just products but experiences.', 'https://www.unno.com'),
(146, 'Transition', 'US', 2001, 'Founded in 2001 by Kyle Young and Kevin Menard, the company is based in Bellingham, Washington, a place renowned for its vibrant mountain biking community.', 'https://www.transitionbikes.com'),
(147, 'Devinci', 'Canada', 1987, 'Felix Gauthier started Devinci Bicycles in 1987 in Chicoutimi, Quebec, Canada.', 'https://www.devinci.com'),
(148, 'Norco', 'Canada', 1964, 'Norco Bicycles, a Canadian company founded in 1964 by Bert Lewis. The name Norco stands for North Shore Company, inspired by the North Shore mountains near Vancouver, which are famous for their challenging mountain bike trails.', 'https://www.norco.com'),
(149, 'Bridgestone', 'Japan', 1931, 'Bridgestone Corporation, founded in 1931 by Shojiro Ishibashi in Japan, initially focused on tire manufacturing. In the 1940s, they diversified into bicycle production, introducing the Anchor brand as a premium line of racing bikes. Anchor, known for its quality and technological innovation, marked Bridgestones foray into the competitive cycling industry.', 'https://www.bscycle.co.jp'),
(150, 'Blackheart', 'US', 2019, 'Founder Zach Lambert saw a need for a single bike that struck the perfect balance between road and gravel bikes, and was better suited for the average cycling enthusiast who didn''t count every gram or measure every watt.Thus, BlackHeart was born.', 'https://blackheartbikeco.com'),
(151, 'Kaze', 'Thailand', 0, 'na', 'https://ridekaze.bike'),
(152, 'Pilot', 'Netherlands', 2010, 'na', 'https://www.pilotcycles.com'),
(153, 'Crescent', 'Sweden', 1894, '1894 the first Crescent bicycle is imported to Sweden from California where we have our roots.', 'https://www.crescent.se'),
(154, 'Sunpeed', 'China', 2012, 'SUNPEED was established in 2012, located in Shenzhen, China. Sun is also the last name of the founder of the brand Xiping Sun.', 'https://www.sunpeed.com'),
(155, 'Cinelli', 'Italy', 1948, 'Cinelli is an Italian bicycle manufacturing company founded in 1948 by Cino Cinelli, a former professional road racer.', 'https://www.cinelli-milano.com'),
(156, 'Bottecchia', 'Italy', 1926, 'The history of Bottecchia bicycles begins with Ottavio Bottecchia, who was Italy''s first Tour de France winner in 1924 and again in 1925. Ottavio''s success and popularity laid the foundation for the brand, which officially started in 1926 when Ottavio and Carnielli, a cycling enthusiast and businessman, founded the company.', 'https://www.bottecchia.com'),
(157, 'Parlee', 'USA', 2000, 'Parlee Cycles, founded in 2000 by Bob Parlee, specializes in high-performance carbon fiber bicycles. Drawing from Bob''s background in boat building, the company innovated in carbon fiber frame design, emphasizing lightweight and responsive bikes. Parlee Cycles is known for its custom, hand-built road bike frames and has expanded its product line to include a variety of road and other cycling models.', 'https://parleecycles.com/products/ouray'),
(158, 'Elilee', '', 0, '', 'https://elilee.com'),
(159, 'Curve', 'Australia', 2012, 'Curve Cycling was founded in 2012 by Steve Varga, who wanted to offer riders high-quality bikes without excessive marketing or high prices. The company is based in Melbourne, Australia, and its goal is to create products that provide new experiences and continue to perform throughout their expected lifespan.', 'https://www.curvecycling.com'),
(160, 'Enigma', 'UK', 2006, 'Enigma Bikes, a British bicycle manufacturer, was founded in 2006 by Jim Walker. Known for its high-quality titanium and steel frames, Enigma has established itself as a reputable brand in the cycling industry. The company focuses on crafting bespoke and semi-custom bicycles, combining traditional craftsmanship with modern technology. Enigma Bikes has gained recognition for its attention to detail, performance-oriented designs, and commitment to customer satisfaction. Over the years, Enigma has built a loyal following among cyclists who appreciate the durability, comfort, and performance of their bikes.', 'https://www.enigmabikes.com/'),
(161, 'Fiftyone', 'Ireland', 2016, 'FiftyOne Bikes, founded in 2016 by former professional cyclist Aidan Duff in Dublin, Ireland, specializes in custom-built, high-performance road bikes. Known for meticulous craftsmanship and personalized designs, the company uses advanced technology to create bikes tailored to each rider''s unique needs. Over the years, FiftyOne Bikes has gained a global reputation for quality and innovation in the bespoke cycling industry.', 'https://fiftyonebikes.com'),
(162, 'Merit', 'Czech Republic', 2015, 'Merit Bikes is based in the Czech Republic. The company focuses on designing and producing high-quality gravel bikes and components, tailored for the demands of gravel and adventure riding. Their products are developed with a strong emphasis on performance, durability, and user-friendly design, catering to both professional and amateur cyclists.', 'https://meritbikes.com'),
(163, 'Pivot', 'USA', 2007, 'Pivot Cycles is a high-end bicycle manufacturer based in the U.S., known for its innovation and advanced mountain bike technology. Founded in 2007 by Chris Cocalis, a veteran in the cycling industry, Pivot Cycles quickly established a reputation for producing top-tier mountain bikes with cutting-edge suspension designs and geometry.', 'https://www.pivotcycles.com'),
(164, 'XDS', 'China', 1995, 'XDS (Xidesheng), established in 1995 in Shenzhen, China, is one of the world’s largest bicycle manufacturers, producing millions of frames annually, including cutting-edge carbon fiber models. Over the years, XDS has grown from a regional player into a global powerhouse, leveraging advanced manufacturing techniques and extensive research and development. In 2025, the company elevated its profile by introducing X-LAB, its premium sub-brand focused on high-performance bicycles. X-LAB gained significant attention when it partnered with the Astana cycling team, rebranding it as XDS-Astana and supplying the X-LAB AD9, an aero road bike developed with input from experts like Alex Dowsett. This marked the first entry of a Chinese frame manufacturer into WorldTour cycling, solidifying XDS and X-LAB as leaders in both mass-market and elite cycling.', 'https://www.xdsbicycles.com.au/pages/technology'),
(165, 'WKNDR', 'UK', 2009, 'Founded in 2009 by Ricky Feather in York, England, Feather Cycles emerged from Ricky''s background as a professional industrial welder and BMX rider to become a pinnacle of the British bespoke bicycle scene. Known for exquisite craftsmanship, hand-carved lugs, and a mastery of high-end steel, the brand gained international acclaim through collaborations with Rapha and multiple "Best in Show" awards at Bespoked.', 'https://wkndr.cc');
